# California Rolls

Based on [https://makemysushi.com/Recipes/…](https://makemysushi.com/Recipes/how-to-make-california-sushi-rolls) ([wayback](http://web.archive.org/web/20250911093743/https://makemysushi.com/Recipes/how-to-make-california-sushi-rolls))

{ rating="3" image="california_rolls.jpeg" }
:::
:::

## Ingredients

- [ ] 6 sticks [Surimi]{ ing="surimi" } (Imitation crab)
- [ ] 1/2 [avocado]{ ing="avocado" }
- [ ] [cucumber]{ ing="cucumber" }
- [ ] [sesame seeds]{ ing="sesame-seeds" }
- [ ] [sushi rice]{ ing="sushi-rice" }
- [ ] [Nori]{ ing="nori" }
- [ ] [Masago]{ ing="masago" } (flying fish roe) or Tobiko

## Recipe

1. Cut the [Nori]{ ing="nori" } sheet in half. Spread [rice]{ ing="sushi-rice" } over the Nori and top with [sesame seeds]{ ing="sesame-seeds" }, then flip rice side down
1. Add strips of the [Surimi]{ ing="surimi" }, [avocado]{ ing="avocado" }, [cucumber]{ ing="cucumber" }, and choice of fish roe then roll

## Notes

1. Tobiko is fish eggs with corn syrup and food coloring
1. See more [detailed guide here](https://www.justonecookbook.com/california-roll) ([wayback](http://web.archive.org/web/20251201021329/https://www.justonecookbook.com/california-roll/))
